  "verbalization": "Mesoridazine, a phenothiazine antipsychotic, is consistently linked to Htr6 through a shared lineage in the Phenothiazines class. The evidence suggests that Mesoridazine, as part of this class, binds to Htr6 through its inclusion in the broader antipsychotic agent category. This relationship is reinforced by the presence of multiple phenothiazine derivatives—Perphenazine, Fluphenazine, and Trifluoperazine—all of which exhibit a binding interaction with Htr6. The lowest common ancestors across these paths indicate a shared classification in the Phenothiazines group, suggesting a common mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Mesoridazine in modulating Htr6 activity, likely through its antipsychotic properties. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Mesoridazine and Htr6, mediated by the phenothiazine class, and underscores the importance of this relationship in understanding its pharmacological effects.",
